        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: B-Sides Ultra\n- People: Iggy Pop, David Bowie, Lou Reed, John Cale, Sterling Morrison, Angus MacLise, Moe Tucker\n- Organizations: The Velvet Underground\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: cover songs, rock bands\n\nFacts:\n- In 1964, The Velvet Underground was formed in New York City.\n- In 1964, The Velvet Underground was formed by Lou Reed, John Cale, Sterling Morrison, and Angus MacLise.\n- In 1965, Moe Tucker replaced Angus MacLise in The Velvet Underground.\n- B-Sides Ultra contains two cover songs.\n- B-Sides Ultra includes a version of \"China Girl,\" a song by Iggy Pop and David Bowie.\n- B-Sides Ultra includes a version of The Velvet Underground's \"Sunday Morning\".",
